{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01PdVc1TZ99JgqszEd9XWnxA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ERRORS.md — Phase A error-surface table\n2\t\n3\t## How this table was derived\n4\t\n5\t`c_src/src/main.c` is 45 lines and contains **no** `RETURN_ERROR` macro, no\n6\t`assert`, no `return -1`, no `return NULL`, no error enum and no explicit range\n7\tor null check:\n8\t\n9\t```\n10\t$ grep -nE 'return|assert|NULL|if |else|while |for ' c_src/src/main.c\n11\t28:    for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n12\t44:    return 0;\n13\t```\n14\t\n15\tThe program's entire rejection surface therefore lives in the *one* library\n16\tcall that can fail and whose result the C code deliberately **ignores**:\n17\t\n18\t```c\n19\tint main() {\n20\t    float x = 0.f;      /* <- the value that survives every rejection */\n21\t    scanf(\"%f\", &x);    /* return value ignored: no assignment on failure */\n22\t    driver(x);\n23\t    return 0;\n24\t}\n25\t```\n26\t\n27\tConsequently **every rejection has the same observable effect**: `x` keeps its\n28\tinitialiser `0.f`, so the program prints `00000000` and exits 0.  Note this is\n29\t*positive* zero — the sign of a rejected `\"-…\"` input is **not** applied,\n30\tbecause glibc keeps the leading sign out of the buffer it hands to `strtof`\n31\tand only negates *after* a successful conversion.\n32\t\n33\tThe rows below enumerate every distinct condition under which glibc's `%f`\n34\tconversion rejects its input.  They were derived from the character-collection\n35\tstate machine in glibc's `__vfscanf_internal` (the `case L_('e')` float arm)\n36\tand each one was then *confirmed against the compiled C program* — the\n37\t`expected C result` column is the C binary's actual output, not a guess.\n38\t\n39\t`ERANGE` results (overflow/underflow) are included because `scanf` still\n40\t*assigns* in those cases; they are error-ish outcomes rather than rejections.\n41\t\n42\t## Table\n43\t\n44\t| #  | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n45\t|----|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n46\t| 1  | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | empty stdin — EOF before any character (*input failure*) | no assignment; `x == +0.0f`; prints `00000000`, exit 0 |\n47\t| 2  | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | stdin is whitespace only (`\" \\t\\n\\v\\f\\r\"`) — EOF while skipping whitespace | `00000000`, exit 0 |\n48\t| 3  | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | EOF immediately after a leading sign (`\"-\"`, `\"+\"`) | `00000000` (**not** `00000080`), exit 0 |\n49\t| 4  | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | first non-space character cannot start a number and is not `n`/`i` (`\"z\"`, `\"_\"`, `\",\"`, `\"(\"`, `\"e5\"`, `\"E\"`, `\"*\"`) → collection buffer stays empty | `00000000`, exit 0 |\n50\t| 5  | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | a second sign directly after the first (`\"--1\"`, `\"+-1\"`, `\"-+\"`) | `00000000`, exit 0 |\n51\t| 6  | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | NUL byte or byte ≥ 0x80 as the first non-space character (`\"\\0\"`, `\"\\x80\"`, `\"\\xff\"`, UTF-8 `\"π\"`) | `00000000`, exit 0 |\n52\t| 7  | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | `n`/`N` not followed by `a`/`A` (`\"n\"`, `\"nx\"`, `\"n5\"`, `\"N\"`) | `00000000`, exit 0 |\n53\t| 8  | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | `na` not followed by `n`/`N` (`\"na\"`, `\"nax\"`, `\"na5\"`, `\"-na\"`) | `00000000`, exit 0 |\n54\t| 9  | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | `i`/`I` not followed by `n`/`N` (`\"i\"`, `\"ix\"`, `\"i5\"`) | `00000000`, exit 0 |\n55\t| 10 | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | `in` not followed by `f`/`F` (`\"in\"`, `\"inx\"`, `\"in5\"`, `\"-in\"`) | `00000000`, exit 0 |\n56\t| 11 | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | `inf` followed by `i`/`I` but **not** the complete word `infinity` (`\"infi\"`, `\"infin\"`, `\"infini\"`, `\"infinit\"`, `\"infix\"`, `\"infinit1\"`, `\"-infin\"`) — glibc commits to the long spelling and then fails | `00000000`, exit 0 |\n57\t| 12 | `main`/`scanf(\"%f\")` | `0x`/`0X` prefix followed by EOF (`\"0x\"`, `\"0X\"`,