t| 21 | `driver` (FFI) | out-of-range \"enum-like\" integer reinterpreted as a float — every one of the 2^32 bit patterns is a valid argument, there is no rejection path | byte-exact echo of the pattern (no NaN canonicalisation) |\n67\t| 22 | `print_hex` (internal) | `len == 0` would print only `\"\\n\"`; unreachable from the public API because `driver` always passes `sizeof(float) == 4` | n/a — fixed at 4, verified by the 4-byte output width |\n68\t\n69\t## Checklist\n70\t\n71\t| # | differential test | status |\n72\t|---|-------------------|--------|\n73\t| 1  | `tests/error_paths.rs::eof_and_whitespace_only` | [x] |\n74\t| 2  | `tests/error_paths.rs::eof_and_whitespace_only` | [x] |\n75\t| 3  | `tests/error_paths.rs::eof_after_sign` | [x] |\n76\t| 4  | `tests/error_paths.rs::first_char_cannot_start_a_number` | [x] |\n77\t| 5  | `tests/error_paths.rs::double_sign` | [x] |\n78\t| 6  | `tests/error_paths.rs::non_ascii_and_nul_bytes` | [x] |\n79\t| 7  | `tests/error_paths.rs::nan_word_truncated` | [x] |\n80\t| 8  | `tests/error_paths.rs::nan_word_truncated` | [x] |\n81\t| 9  | `tests/error_paths.rs::inf_word_truncated` | [x] |\n82\t| 10 | `tests/error_paths.rs::inf_word_truncated` | [x] |\n83\t| 11 | `tests/error_paths.rs::inf_commits_to_infinity` | [x] |\n84\t| 12 | `tests/error_paths.rs::hex_prefix_only` | [x] |\n85\t| 13 | `tests/error_paths.rs::hex_prefix_then_non_hex` | [x] |\n86\t| 14 | `tests/error_paths.rs::hex_prefix_then_exponent_char` | [x] |\n87\t| 15 | `tests/error_paths.rs::lone_decimal_point` | [x] |\n88\t| 16 | `tests/error_paths.rs::overflow_to_infinity` | [x] |\n89\t| 17 | `tests/error_paths.rs::underflow_to_zero` | [x] |\n90\t| 18 | `tests/error_paths.rs::exponent_without_digits` | [x] |\n91\t| 19 | `tests/error_paths.rs::trailing_garbage_stops_scan` | [x] |\n92\t| 20 | `tests/ffi_driver_diff.rs::ffi_differential_suite` (named-specials section) | [x] |\n93\t| 21 | `tests/ffi_driver_diff.rs::ffi_differential_suite` (exhaustive + random bit patterns)