{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VXCMenbMNwjJnTsf2Y8BqY","type":"tool_result","content":"=== c_src source untouched? ===\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 1261 Aug 18 10:56 c_src/CMakeLists.txt\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 1536 Aug 18 10:56 c_src/src/main.c\n61ed8a676f9a90a87533f242ef663084  c_src/src/main.c\na535940e660ba650181606297f65903d  c_src/CMakeLists.txt\n\n=== Cargo.toml ===\n[package]\nname = \"driver\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[[bin]]\nname = \"driver\"\npath = \"src/main.rs\"\n\n# C-ABI shared library mirroring the symbols that c_src/src/main.c exports when\n# built with `gcc -shared` (`driver`, `main`).  Used by the differential tests\n# in tests/, which dlopen both this .so and the C .so via libloading.\n[lib]\nname = \"driver\"\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n\n[profile.release]\npanic = \"abort\"\n\n[workspace]\n\n=== artifacts ===\n-rwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon 466048 Aug 18 11:34 target/release/driver\n-rwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon 433992 Aug 18 11:34 target/release/libdriver.so\n\ncbuild/:\ntotal 7788\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 scheschb amazon   15968 Aug 18 11:39 libcdriver.so\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 scheschb amazon 3996496 Aug 18 11:26 libdriver_rustc_debug.so\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 scheschb amazon 3957656 Aug 18 11:27 libdriver_rustc_release.so\n\n=== FINAL symbol diff (must be empty) ===\n<<<end>>>\n\n=== smoke ===\n0000c03f vs 0000c03f\n00000000 vs 00000000\n00000000 vs 00000000\n0000c07f vs 0000c07f\n00000000 vs 00000000\n00004040 vs 00004040","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6d65dbd-014f-430d-a248-aed6264b096a","uuid":"d31519c1-0f0b-4b79-bfdc-15c054c97570","timestamp":"2026-08-18T11:41:25.885Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== c_src source untouched? ===\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 1261 Aug 18 10:56 c_src/CMakeLists.txt\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 1536 Aug 18 10:56 c_src/src/main.c\n61ed8a676f9a90a87533f242ef663084  c_src/src/main.c\na535940e660ba650181606297f65903d  c_src/CMakeLists.txt\n\n=== Cargo.toml ===\n[package]\nname = \"driver\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[[bin]]\nname = \"driver\"\npath = \"src/main.rs\"\n\n# C-ABI shared library mirroring the symbols that c_src/src/main.c exports when\n# built with `gcc -shared` (`driver`, `main`).  Used by the differential tests\n# in tests/, which dlopen both this .so and the C .so via libloading.\n[lib]\nname = \"driver\"\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n\n[profile.release]\npanic = \"abort\"\n\n[workspace]\n\n=== artifacts ===\n-rwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon 466048 Aug 18 11:34 target/release/driver\n-rwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon 433992 Aug 18 11:34 target/release/libdriver.so\n\ncbuild/:\ntotal 7788\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 scheschb amazon   15968 Aug 18 11:39 libcdriver.so\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 scheschb amazon 3996496 Aug 18 11:26 libdriver_rustc_debug.so\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 scheschb amazon 3957656 Aug 18 11:27 libdriver_rustc_release.so\n\n=== FINAL symbol diff (must be empty) ===\n<<<end>>>\n\n=== smoke ===\n0000c03f vs 0000c03f\n00000000 vs 00000000\n00000000 vs 00000000\n0000c07f vs 0000c07f\n00000000 vs 00000000\n00004040 vs 00004040","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pcx5cml7xxi7t3dauwla3kliin4hkohlmoet4yds3od7urmgmxhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. Everything passes.\n\n## What the C program is\n\n`c_src/` is an **executable** (`add_executable(driver src/main.c)`), 45 lines: `scanf(\"%f\", &x)` into a `float x = 0.f`, then `driver(x)` dumps the 4 raw bytes as lowercase hex + `\\n`. The only non-`static` symbols are `driver` and `main`.\n\n## Bugs found and fixed in the Rust (3 real divergences)\n\nThe original translation hand-rolled a `strtof`-style tokenizer. But glibc's `scanf(\"%f\")` uses a **different** character-collection state machine than `strtof`, so it rejects inputs `strtof` accepts:\n\n| input | C (ground truth) | old Rust | cause |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `-0x` | `00000000` (+0) | `00000080` (−0) | glibc keeps the sign *out* of the buffer given to `strtof`; a buffer of exactly `\"0x\"` is a **conversion failure**, so `x` keeps its `+0.f` initialiser. Same for `-0xg`, `-0xp1`, `-0x,`, `-0x-`, `-0x+`, `-0x_` |\n| `infin` | `00000000` | `0000807f` (inf) | once `inf` is followed by `i`, glibc **commits** to the full word `infinity` and fails otherwise (`infi`, `infin`, `infini`, `infinit`, `infix`, `infinit1`) |\n| `infinit` | `00000000` | inf | same |\n\n`src/scan.rs` now reproduces glibc's collector faithfully (sign held separately, `\"0x\"`-only buffer rejected, exponent char only accepted after a digit, `\".\"`-only buffer rejected, `nan(payload)` not consumed).\n\n## Structure changes\n\n- `src/scan.rs` — shared implementation; `src/main.rs` — bin; `src/lib.rs` — `cdylib` exporting `#[no_mangle] driver` and `main`, so both `.so`s can be `dlopen`ed side by side. `cargo build --release` still produces an identical-behaving `target/release/driver`.\n- Added `libloading = \"0.8\"` to `[dev-dependencies]`. `c_src/` sources untouched (md5 verified).\n\n## Phase results\n\n- **A** — `SYMBOLS.md` / `ERRORS.md` (22 rows) / `CONFIGS.md` (30 rows), all mechanically derived from the C source.\n- **B** — 26 tests, one per CONFIGS row group, randomized with fixed seeds: all pass.\n- **C** — 19 error-path tests; each asserts the *concrete* sentinel (`00000000\\n`, exit 0) rather than \"both failed\". All pass. Three initial failures were **my wrong expectations** (`0xe` is 14.0 since `e` is a hex digit; `infinIty2` is accepted; `1.5e5e5` → 150000) — C and Rust never disagreed.\n- **D** — `nm -D` C→Rust symbol diff is **empty**; `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and `main.c` has 0 `#ifdef`s, so the single configuration was verified via `tools/check_features.sh` under `--no-default-features`, default, and `--all-features`, in both debug and release.\n\nSupplementary sweeps (`tools/`): ~140k randomized + ~98k exhaustive short-string cases (`len ≤ 5` over `0x.p1e+-`, hex and word alphabets), exact ½-ulp midpoints via bignum decimal, 100k-digit inputs — **0 mismatches**."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1489,"cache_read_input_tokens":215897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1489,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6d65dbd-014f-430d-a248-aed6264b096a","uuid":"253a04be-f0fe-4d0b-809f-b7d3b154b2cb","timestamp":"2026-08-18T11:41:52.772Z"}
